{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/270467-shameless-plug-kickstarter-for-chill-is-live","id":270467,"title":"[Shameless plug]Kickstarter for Chill is live","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-01T16:22:08-07:00","id":270467,"title":"[Shameless plug]Kickstarter for Chill is live","content":"What, you think I just write OPP games? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Our Kickstarter for <b>Chill 3rd Edition</b> just launched <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/playattentiongames/chill-3rd-edition-a-horror-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I'm happy to answer questions or convince you to back however I can, including giving random <b>Beast</b> spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T16:56:56-07:00","id":270482,"title":"","content":"Growling Doors has never disappointed me before. Backed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T01:51:19-07:00","id":271485,"title":"","content":"Still have the Swedish translation of the first edition in my RPG collection. While mechanics like how the Chill tookens is described tend to make an rpg feel far too much of a game for me, Chill was probably the first game I started to ignore rules as written and started modify them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So, I have already backed it. Looking forward to see how this version will turn out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T03:44:28-07:00","id":271515,"title":"","content":"What we've found in play is that the Chill tokens provide a way for players to hedge their bets, much in the same way Willpower does in the WoD systems. And, of course, there's the nice tension build when the CM adds a chip. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T04:38:35-07:00","id":271548,"title":"","content":"There is two genres I'm definitely not good at GMing; one is comedy and the other is horror. But there are a few times I have managed to pull off a horror game. One major part of those times, beside letting the players imagination work against themselves, has been to make sure they feel control is just out of their grasp. Being able to hedge their bets tend to work against that (I generally uses that kind of system when I want action). Building tension by adding chips have never fitted my preference, but I might be pleasantly surprised (I prefer to use their failed rolls to build tension by giving them a new chance to succeed, but having them hearing some noise slowly getting closer, and closer, and closer...).<br /> <br /> But I know people who loves that kind of system. There is no system that will fit everyone, and I can always mod it with house-rules so it will fit me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}